<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "boot.ready.warning">
<!ENTITY author "Ray Munro">
<!ENTITY version "2026.09.14a">
<!ENTITY emhttp "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY github "RayMunro/unraid-boot-ready-notify">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/&name;.plg">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" min="6.12.0" icon="boot.ready.warning.png"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        support="https://github.com/&github;/issues"
        project="https://github.com/&github;"
        readme="https://github.com/&github;#readme">

<CHANGES>
### 2026.09.14a
- Fix the install-success message printing a hardcoded old version number instead of the version actually installed (the message lived inside a CDATA install script, so the &amp;version; entity was never expanded there).

### 2026.09.14
- Add a copyright notice to the README shown in the Plugins tab, matching the other HackerHog plugins.

### 2026.09.02f
- Fixes the recurring black-bell problem by verifying icon metadata after Unraid finishes its native plugin-registration step.
- Uses a delayed post-install finalizer because Unraid copies/registers the .plg only after the plugin install payload returns.
- Removes duplicate Plugin Manager registrations for the same internal plugin identity.
- Moves duplicate persistent boot.ready.warning definitions to plugins-stale so an older copy cannot restore old icon metadata at the next boot.
- Distribution filename is versioned to prevent a Mac browser from leaving a newer download as "(1)" while copy commands accidentally reuse an older file.
- Keeps the custom PNG icon, Warning severity, native started-event trigger, Docker readiness gate, and once-per-boot behaviour.

### 2026.09.02e
- Permanently fixes Plugin Manager registration by recreating the native /var/log/plugins symlink during every install.
- Adds a repair-registration helper script and invokes it automatically.
- Uninstall now removes the registration symlink as well as runtime files.
- Keeps the custom PNG icon, Warning severity, native started-event trigger, Docker readiness gate, and once-per-boot behaviour.

### 2026.09.02d
- Adds a native custom PNG icon for the Unraid Plugins tab.
- Installs the icon under the plugin images directory with a transparent background.
- Adds a friendly README description displayed by Unraid Plugin Manager.
- Boot trigger, Docker readiness gate, Warning severity, and once-per-boot behaviour are unchanged.

### 2026.09.02c
- Uses a new internal plugin identity to avoid Unraid's stale same-plugin registration.
- Removes stale files/runtime from the earlier boot.ready.notify builds during install.
- Sends boot-ready and test notifications with Warning severity.
- Uses Unraid's native started event and waits for Docker readiness.
</CHANGES>

<!-- Prepare a clean runtime. This is a NEW plugin identity, but remove stale
     runtime/flash entries from the earlier builds so they cannot fire too. -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
set -e

pkill -f '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/boot.ready.notify/scripts/boot-ready-worker' 2>/dev/null || true
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/boot.ready.notify
rm -rf /run/boot.ready.notify
rm -f /var/log/boot-ready-notify.log

# Remove only the OLD plugin definitions/registration markers.
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/boot-ready-notify.plg
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/boot.ready.notify.plg
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/boot.ready.notify
rm -f /var/log/plugins/boot-ready-notify.plg
rm -f /var/log/plugins/boot.ready.notify.plg

mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/boot.ready.warning/event
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/boot.ready.warning/scripts
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/boot.ready.warning/images
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

